{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Turkish display names for every structure in packages/anatomy-manifest. One file so an expert can check all terms before public release.",
    "status": "Every term is a translation made during development and is marked needs-expert-review. No openly citable official Turkish anatomical terminology list was found (search 2026-11-19). Reviewer reference: FIPAT Terminologia Anatomica 2nd ed. (Latin, freely distributable PDF) https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/",
    "keys": "GLB node name without the VH_M_ prefix. Segment meshes ending in _a/_b use their parent's term.",
    "reviewWorkflow": "Reviewer changes `tr` if needed and sets `status` to `expert-reviewed` plus `reviewer` and `date`.",
    "coverage": "Milestone 4: Turkish terms exist for every structure of the heart, vessels and lungs, and for the top-level and listed structures of the newly added organs. Other new sub-structures fall back to the English source label and are flagged 'Türkçe terim henüz yok' in the app; scripts/report-missing-tr.mjs lists them."
  },
